title: 'pallet-revive: benchmark the EVM `JUMPI` opcode'
doc:
- audience: Runtime Dev
  description: |-
    The EVM interpreter charged every opcode a multiple of the benchmarked cost
    of `JUMPDEST`, scaled by the opcode's Ethereum gas constant. Those charges
    were estimates rather than measurements of the work each opcode does, and
    the August benchmarking results showed them overcharging execution.

    This PR adds an `evm_jumpi_opcode` benchmark and charges `JUMP` and `JUMPI`
    from it instead of the estimate. The benchmark runs `JUMPI` back to back
    with the operands of every jump loaded onto the stack ahead of time, so no
    `PUSH` instructions are measured and nothing has to be subtracted when the
    charge is computed. Every jump is taken, which is the worst case.
    
    A crate-internal `EvmOpcodeCosts` token implementing `Token<T>` yields the
    weight of each benchmarked opcode. This is the groundwork for benchmarking
    the remaining opcodes the same way.

    `WeightInfo` gains `evm_jumpi_opcode`, so runtimes that provide their own
    weights for `pallet-revive` need to regenerate them.
crates:
- name: pallet-revive
  bump: major
- name: asset-hub-westend-runtime
  bump: patch
